{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggFbk89SioZesbd7CPX4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `split_cents` in `money.py`. The leftover grosze are now spread one each across the first few shares, so the parts always add up to the total.\n\n```python\nshare, extra = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + (i < extra) for i in range(people)]\n```\n\nI checked a few cases by hand, and no grosz goes missing in any of them:\n- `split_cents(100, 3)` gives `[34, 33, 33]`.\n- `split_cents(100, 4)` gives `[25, 25, 25, 25]`.\n- `split_cents(2, 5)` gives `[1, 1, 0, 0, 0]`.\n- `split_cents(0, 3)` gives `[0, 0, 0]`.\n\nI wrote no tests, as you asked, so nothing in the repo guards this. I didn't commit anything. The fix took two lines, not the one-liner the tech lead expected.\n\nThe extra grosz always goes to the first person in the list. If whoever pays should absorb it, or the split should rotate, tell me before you deploy. I also haven't checked negative totals, which `divmod` handles differently from a plain `//`.\n\nFor next sprint's tests, start with the sum invariant: `sum(split_cents(t, p)) == t`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":19268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":571},"output_tokens":406,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52f60d29-dd5e-489b-abde-e285b1fd8963","uuid":"76525413-8ac3-4361-81c7-504ffb1a49db","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:44:34.912Z","request_id":"req_011CggFbjukgLsaqATjGtuer"}
